  "unknowns": [
    "Beep length, gap, and what the stored value is at entry: not stated.",
    "What happens after the last value (11) or on a value above the maximum: not stated (wrap-around unknown).",
    "Which models have a sensor connection: not stated; the mode numbers shift for those without.",
    "Stick-menu defaults: not stated. The telemetry menu lists factory settings (battery LiPo, rotation normal, A-Brake 0%), which may match.",
    "The manual states that mode 3 depends on the model type; the model type must be set first.",
    "Calibration timings: melody at about 10 s, motor-off within 4 s (6 s for neutral/brake teach-in)."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Graupner_BrushlessControlPlusT_EN.pdf names the model type as 'mode 4' in its warning text and as mode 5 in the table; Graupner_BrushlessControlPlusT_DE.pdf and Graupner_BrushlessControl_Series_f3x.pdf say mode 5. The table order (model type is row 5) is used here.",
    "Graupner_BrushlessControlPlusT_DE.pdf lists 21 models and omits S3046 (50 A) and S3064 (HV 160 COOL); the other two manuals list all models.",
    "The model-search function (error message 8) is enabled by the trim in Graupner_BrushlessControlPlusT_DE.pdf and by the telemetry setting M.Lost_beep in Graupner_BrushlessControlPlusT_EN.pdf."
  ],
